DESCRIPTION                  = "This table contains bolometric brightness 
                                temperatures from the Diviner Lunar Radiometer
                                Experiment binned at 240 m and 0.25 hours of 
                                local time derived from a compilation of all
                                nadir observations acquired from 5-July-2009 to
                                17-February-2019 with subsolar latitude less
                                than zero degrees (summer season). Columns are 
                                distances from pole (x,y) normalized by mean radius
                                1737.4 km, longitude, latitude, bolometric temperature.
                                Empty bins are omitted.
                                For more information, please see:
                                Williams et al. (2019) 'Seasonal polar
                                temperatures on the Moon', 
                                J. Geophys. Res, 124, 2505-2521.
                               "
